 "differ": [
  {
   "id": "1971",
   "text": "“I might have been mistress! With these rooms I might have now been familiarly acquainted! Instead of viewing them as a stranger, I might have rejoiced in them as my own, and welcomed to them as visitors my uncle and aunt. But, no,”",
   "full": "Narrator",
   "trimmed": "Lizzy"
  },
  {
   "id": "1973",
   "text": "“that could never be; my uncle and aunt would have been lost to me; I should not have been allowed to invite them.”",
   "full": "Narrator",
   "trimmed": "Lizzy"
  },
  {
   "id": "1986",
   "text": "“I have heard much of your master’s fine person,”",
   "full": "Mrs. Reynolds",
   "trimmed": "Mrs. Hill"
  },
  {
   "id": "1988",
   "text": "“it is a handsome face. But, Lizzy, you can tell us whether it is like or not.”",
   "full": "Mrs. Reynolds",
   "trimmed": "Mrs. Hill"
  },
